<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42494" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanctĭmōnĭālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		sanctimonia, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>holy;</i> of Christians, <i>pious</i>, <i>religious</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vita,</span>”
				i. e. <i>a monastic life</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 1, 3, 56</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulier,</span>”
				i. e. <i>a nun</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 1, 2, 13</span></i>
			. —As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanctĭmōnĭālis</span></b> ,
				is, f., <i>a nun</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Aug.
				Ep. 169</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Retract. 2, 22</span></i>.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanctĭmōnĭālĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>holily</i>, <i>piously</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">degere,</span>”
				i. e. <i>in a cloister</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 1, 3, 56</span></i>
			.</div>
